ubword-level tokenization</figcaption></div></figure>
<p>While subword-level tokenization can be complex to implement, it has sev=
eral benefits. First, it leads to a manageable vocabulary size, thus reduci=
ng the cost of the model learning representations for each subword. Second,=
 subword-level tokenization allows the model to represent unfamiliar words =
by decomposing them into known subwords.</p>
