<p>Positional encoding can be achieved through two common methods:</p>
<ul>
<li>Fixed positional encoding</li>
<li>Learned positional encoding</li>
</ul>
<h5 id=3D"fixed-positional-encoding">Fixed positional encoding</h5>
<p>This method uses a fixed function to map a position (an integer) to a fi=
xed-size vector. The original Transformer paper introduced the sine-cosine =
function at different frequencies as its positional encoding function.</p>
