<p>However, relying on the email's body as the sole input is not very effec=
tive, because it is not always possible to predict the next token this way.=
 Imagine a user who wants to reply to an email from John. When the user typ=
es "Dear," the model should, ideally, suggest "John." However, if that info=
rmation is not provided as input, the model cannot predict "John" as the li=
kely next token.</p>
<p>To address this limitation, we include more information in the input. Fo=
r example, we can use the email's subject, the recipient, and previous emai=
ls, if available. This adds depth to the context and helps the model make m=
ore relevant predictions.</p>
