<h4 id=3D"stochastic-sampling">Stochastic sampling</h4>
<p>Stochastic sampling methods introduce randomness into the generation pro=
cess. For example, at each step of token generation, the model samples from=
 the predicted distribution based on the probabilities assigned to each tok=
en. This means that each time text is generated, even with the same initial=
 inputs, the generated text may vary.</p>
<p>Figure 35 shows two instances of sampling using the same initial token "=
How." The first time, the sequence of generated tokens leads to "How are yo=
u,"; the second time, a different sequence is generated using the same init=
ial token due to the randomness inherent in sampling.</p>
